
Produce a value of the following type:
A ceramic tile.
- tileCut (object): How the tile is cut.
- tileSize (object): The size of the tile when laid.
- tileLabels (array): The labels printed on the tile.
- tileColour (object): The chosen colour, if any.
- tileNote (string): A note for the tiler.

The types above refer to the following types:

Cut:
How a tile is cut.
- Straight: Straight edges, to the given dimensions.
- Curved: A round tile of the given diameter in millimetres.


Dimensions:
The size of a tile.
- dimWidth: The width in millimetres.
- dimHeight: The height in millimetres.


Label:
A text printed on a tile.
- labelText: The words that are printed.


Choice Colour:
Either a value was picked, or none was.
- Pick: The picked value.
- Decline: Nothing was picked.


Colour:
A colour of paint.
- Red: Like a post box.
- Green: Like a lawn.

